# Legacy /pulse redirects to / (homepage is Market Pulse since Sep 2026).
/pulse    /    301
/pulse/   /    301

# The homepage linked city pages as href="city/<name>/" - a path that was
# never built. Pages answered 200 with index.html, so the click looked like
# it did nothing; the next click resolved the same relative href against the
# bad path and the chain grew: /city/jaipur/city/pune/city/nashik/. These
# rescue the single-segment URLs that are already in analytics, inbound links
# and anyone's history. The chains fall through to 404.html, which is the
# honest answer for a URL that never existed.
/city/:slug    /gold-rate-today-in-:slug    301
/city/:slug/   /gold-rate-today-in-:slug    301
